---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { url } from '../lib/url';
import { subprocessors as rows } from '../data/trust';

---
<Layout title="Sub-processors" description="The companies that process data for Laissez, what each one sees, where, and whether it is switched on." path="subprocessors/">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1>Sub-processors</h1>
      <p class="lede">Every company that handles data on Laissez’s behalf, what it sees, where it runs, and whether it is switched on today. If a vendor is not on this page, it does not touch your data.</p>
      <p class="updated">Last updated 7 October 2026.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table class="grid">
          <thead><tr><th scope="col">Provider</th><th scope="col">What it does for Laissez</th><th scope="col">What it sees</th><th scope="col">Where</th><th scope="col">Status</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            {rows.map((r) => (
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">{r.name}</th>
                <td>{r.purpose}{r.note ? <span class="fine" style="display:block;margin-top:0.35rem">{r.note}</span> : null}</td>
                <td>{r.data}</td>
                <td>{r.where}</td>
                <td>{r.status}</td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <div class="prose" style="margin-top:2.5rem">
        <h2>How changes are made</h2>
        <p>A new sub-processor that handles customer data is added to this page before it is used. Customers with a signed data processing agreement are told by email at least 30 days ahead and can object; the <a href={url('dpa/')}>data processing agreement draft</a> sets out the process. Sandboxes contain only fictional data, so they are not covered by that notice.</p>
        <h2>What the statuses mean</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Active</strong>: in use on the live deployment today.</li>
          <li><strong>When enabled</strong>: built and tested, switched on when the deployment is configured for production. Until then it sees nothing.</li>
          <li><strong>Optional</strong>: used only if an organization or the operator turns the feature on.</li>
          <li><strong>Not yet deployed</strong>: planned and not live.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Questions, or a request to subscribe to changes: <a href="mailto:parikshit.ambhore@rice.edu">parikshit.ambhore@rice.edu</a>. See also the <a href={url('privacy/')}>privacy page</a> and the <a href={url('trust/')}>trust page</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
<style>
  .table-wrap { overflow-x: auto; }
  .table-wrap table { min-width: 52rem; }
</style>
